1) Order State Machine — crisp, auditable, idempotent
Core ideas

One row per order in public.trader_orders. Mutate status + append events.

Immutable event log in public.trader_order_events for forensics.

Idempotency keys so retries don’t duplicate.

Separation of concerns:

Consumer (reads intents, validates, writes ACK).

OrderManager (risk check → route → update status).

BrokerAdapter (sim/alpaca/ib… returns external IDs, fills, rejects).

States (minimal but expressive)

ACK – intent accepted by Trader (parsed + persisted).

REJECTED – failed risk / validation (final).

ROUTING – being sent to a broker (transient).

PENDING – accepted by broker, waiting fill/cancel.

PARTIAL – partially filled.

FILLED – fully filled (final).

CANCELED – canceled by us or broker (final).

ERROR – operational failure (retryable depending on error).

Transitions (happy path)

ACK → ROUTING → PENDING → (PARTIAL)* → FILLED

Transitions (sad paths)

ACK → REJECTED (risk says nope)

ROUTING → ERROR (adapter down / 5xx) → backoff → retry → ROUTING/PENDING

PENDING → CANCELED (cancel request or broker cancel)

PENDING/PARTIAL → ERROR (dropout) → recover to PENDING via broker poll

Tables (lean + durable)

public.trader_orders (you already have the core)

id bigserial pk

instance_id text (e.g., liveA)

intent_id text unique (ULID/UUID from evaluator to ensure idempotency)

symbol text, side text, qty int, price numeric(18,6)

status text not null

broker text null (e.g., sim, alpaca)

broker_order_id text null

error text null

payload jsonb null (original intent + enrichments)

created_at timestamptz default now()

updated_at timestamptz default now()

public.trader_order_events

id bigserial pk

order_id bigint references trader_orders(id)

ts timestamptz default now()

event text (ACK, ROUTING, SENT, PENDING, PARTIAL, FILL, CANCEL, ERROR)

details jsonb (adapter response, fill qty/price, error, etc.)

On every status change: update trader_orders.status, bump updated_at, and insert a row into trader_order_events.

Idempotency & retries

Evaluator includes intent_id in the message. Trader does:

if intent_id exists → no new row; optionally re-emit same status.

Routing retries: exponential backoff with jitter, cap attempts, then ERROR with reason but keep polling broker by broker_order_id if known.

Poison handling: if parsing fails → REJECTED with error = 'parse'.

Concurrency control

Single writer per order_id. Use UPDATE … WHERE id = $1 AND status = $expected to avoid stomps, or SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED in a work queue.

Broker callbacks (webhooks/polls) funnel through OrderManager.apply_event(order_id, evt) to keep transitions legal.

